Common school-event games (quick notes)
- Bean bag toss (cornhole-style)
  - Low setup, works for all ages, minimal supervision, needs boards or targets and bean bags.
- Ring toss
  - Compact, easy, low cost, good for younger kids.
- Duck pond (prize-pick from water tub)
  - Simple for young kids, needs small prizes and a tub.
- Balloon pop (prizes inside balloons)
  - Exciting, needs balloons and small prizes, higher prep time.
- Cake walk (musical elimination with numbered spots)
  - Fun for mixed ages, needs music and prizes.
- Sack race / three-legged race
  - Active, needs space and adult supervision.
- Scavenger/treasure hunt
  - Engaging for older kids, needs planning and clues.
- Musical chairs / freeze dance
  - Minimal supplies, good for mixed ages, short rounds.
- Spin-the-wheel / prize wheel
  - Eye-catching, needs a wheel or spinner and prize list.
- Fishing pond (magnetic fish on poles)
  - Good for younger kids, reusable props, low physical risk.
- Ring toss on bottles / milk bottle knockdown
  - Low cost, easy to prep, scalable.
- Trivia / quiz booth
  - Good for older kids and adults, requires questions and a host.
- Obstacle course
  - High energy, needs space and setup, great for outdoors.

